-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/10b34313-45be-4f95-bc19-c4301ee0b2ce
-- title:
--   Frozen rational entropy data for all63 positive DWZ fourth-component regions
-- statement:
--   Exact rational data for the three original regions of each of the 21 positive fourth-power components of the DWZ $q=5$ candidate. The 63 entries are ordered by the released zero-based consumer ID, then region $0,1,2$; `consumerId` and `regionId` record the association. Each entry uses its actual ordered split support, with no padded or duplicated support cells, and supplies a rational split distribution $\alpha$, a separately normalized positive reference $y$, additive coordinate potentials $g$, an error allowance $\varepsilon$, and
--
--   $$U=-\sum_a\alpha_a g_a+\varepsilon.$$
--
--   Coordinate alphabets are embedded in grades $0,\ldots,4$; any unused coordinate-potential grades are zero. Cell counts vary from four to ten, so the reference positivity requirement concerns exactly the actual cells. Dyadic scales and log parameters are rational witnesses for separately proved logarithmic inequalities. These are only data definitions: they assert neither entropy optimality nor tensor extraction. The intended theorem is $H(\rho)\le U$ for every probability distribution with the same three marginals as the corresponding $\alpha$. The paired X/Y-swapped regions reuse these entropy bounds by relabeling, which must be justified when assembling the actual component inequality. The small consumer10 region-weight retune does not change any of these split distributions or entropy duals.
-- source:
--   Duan, Wu, Zhou, Faster Matrix Multiplication via Asymmetric Hashing, https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.10173v5, Equation (34), printed p.71. Released fourth-power data https://osf.io/dta6p/, power4_dup_2.371919.mat SHA256 2aa5713eb352bc94c939d340743c4107b42d274c9fa2058ff879cd7603142aeb. Derived from the frozen exact rational candidate ddf3a94b5a5e1a8ba97b2a385a52675aa0be2f33a77786565098cf30231da10a, with 63 independent positive-reference dual witnesses. The data do not certify full feasibility or omega<2.37193.

